🎯 Challenge: 2-Site OSPF Network
Topology
        R1 (Site A) ── 10.10.10.0/30 ── R2 (Site B)
Dalawang router lang, isang direktang link sa pagitan nila (point-to-point OSPF).

Site A — R1
Base Network: 192.168.10.0/24
Native Trunking VLAN: 100
2 VLAN IDs

VLAN ID	Name	Hosts Needed
10	SALES	25
20	ADMIN	10
Site B — R2
Base Network: 192.168.20.0/24
Native Trunking VLAN: 100
2 VLAN IDs

VLAN ID	Name	Hosts Needed
30	OPS	50
40	GUEST	15
OSPF Link
Link	Network	R1	R2
R1 ↔ R2	10.10.10.0/30	10.10.10.1	10.10.10.2

Gagawin mo (buong flow)
1. VLSM Computation — hatiin yung 192.168.10.0/24 (Site A) at 192.168.20.0/24 (Site B)
papunta sa 2 subnets base sa host requirement bawat isa (malaki muna bago maliit)

2. VLAN Creation + Port Assigning + Trunking — sa switches mo (Native VLAN 100)

3. Router Subinterfaces — Eth1/0.10, .20 (Site A) at Eth1/0.30, .40 (Site B), gamit yung gateway
IP mula sa VLSM computation mo
4. DHCP Pools — per VLAN, i-exclude yung gateway
5. Inter-Router Link — 10.10.10.1/30 sa R1, 10.10.10.2/30 sa R2 (walang kailangang i-VLSM pa dito)
6. OSPF Config — network statements para sa inter-router link AT sa apat na LAN subnets
(network + wildcard lang, hindi interface name)
7. Verify — show ip ospf neighbor, show ip route ospf
8. Test — ping mula PC sa Site A papunta PC sa Site B

==================================================================================================
CLI Commands

Site A

@Access Switch(L2)
create VLANS, port assignment, trunking(custom native vlan is used)

@Trunking Core Switch
create VLANS, trunking(custom native vlan is used)

-------------------------------------------
@Router(R1)
1. Create the SVIS and subinterface
SVI for LAN subinterfaces
conf t
int port#.VLAN-ID
encapsulation dot1q VLAN-ID#
ip address 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.224
ip nat inside
no shut
end

for OSPF port
conf t
int port#
ip address 10.10.10.1 255.255.255.252
no shut
end

2. Create IP DHCP POOL in each VLANS
IP DHCP POOL
conf t
network 192.168.10.0 255.255.255.224
default-router 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.224
dns-server 8.8.8.8
domain-name NAME.COM
ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.10.1 192.168.10.30 !optional
end

!for OPSF Link Configurations
!note the network and wildcard neighbor is mus be inputed not the device of the configuring device
meaning the other devices

@R1 link to R2 and Site-A Coreswitch
conf t
router ospf 1
log-adjancency-changes
network 10.10.10.0 0.0.0.3 area 0 !(Area 0 is the backbone of each site)
network 192.168.10.0 0.0.0 0.0.0.31 area 0
end
